    # v407 (03/11/2026) -- THE PSION, THE CORNER AND THE PAIR: 9 new modules in the kernel (PsionCanto, Par and the seven stones of 02/11 with ratified names); the lemma of the two faces and the key that used to link the two faces, READ from the kernel of the rite; the bound pair, which never cancels; the reservations stated. The numbers come from the core of this rite, never typed.
    # The top frame (The Single-Word Test, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule is not touched. Nothing here moves the gate. Kernel validity is not creditation.
    _rg407 = ("psion_canto_v407", "cunhagens_v407", "kh_n1_cobertura_v407")
    _ok407 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in _rg407)
    _f407 = core.get("psion_canto_v407") or {}
    _v407 = _f407.get("values") or {}
    _ch407 = _f407.get("keys") or {}
    _el407 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cvr407 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _td407 = (globals().get("_V407_PSION_CONTRACT") or {}).get("teste_d") or {}
    _i407 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _b407 = lambda x_: (r"\textsf{True}" if x_ is True else r"\textsf{False}" if x_ is False else r"\text{n/a}")
    _tx407 = lambda x_: "n/a" if x_ is None else str(x_).replace(chr(92), "").replace("_", r"\_\allowbreak{}")
    s.append(r"\section*{The psion and the corner: the passage under compression, and the pair}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The psion and the corner: the passage under compression, and the pair}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the v407 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok407 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{The order.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 03/11/2026 (our translation; the Portuguese is the quotation): how can we test the condition I mentioned; the lemma that links the psion to the corner can also be derived by now; let us go ahead with everything, I ratify everything; and, naming: I agree with the name (the stone \texttt{PsionCanto}), ``Par'' (the stone of the pair) and I agree with all the names and ratify them (the seven stones of 02/11). "
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} " + _i407(_v407.get("n_modulos")) + r" new modules in the kernel, under \texttt{TGLExt/}: \texttt{PsionCanto}, \texttt{Par}, \texttt{APonteDoAtrito}, \texttt{OUmInscrito}, \texttt{KEhATangente}, \texttt{AChaveDaGuarda}, \texttt{OGuarda}, \texttt{LeituraPreservada} and \texttt{OIgual}, with the operator's names; "
             + _i407(_v407.get("n_flags")) + r" flags, named declarations only; the kernel ladder closes at " + _i407(_el407.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i407(_el407.get("n_theorems_expected")) + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage reads " + _i407(_cvr407.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i407(_cvr407.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. The v406 stones and records \emph{stay as they are}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The condition, read under compression.} \textsf{[REAL]} The corner of the psion on the Fock face is the projection onto the line of the vacuum. It is proved, for every Fock certificate and, without hypothesis, in the v406 inhabitant (\texttt{physicalFockCertificate}): the corner \emph{scalarises} ($P\,y\,P=\langle\psi,y\psi\rangle\,P$); $\langle\psi,\Delta^{it}\psi\rangle=1$; and $P\,\Delta^{it}\,P=P$, that is, the Jones reading of the modular flow of the light (the continuous side, type~III) through the corner returns the corner itself (\texttt{jones\_reading\_of\_the\_light\_is\_the\_corner}); the Jones contraction (the measurement on the finite side) and the flow of the light read the same thing in the corner (\texttt{the\_two\_motors\_agree\_in\_the\_corner}). "
             r"\textsf{[ONTO]} This is what the operator called working under compression; what the kernel delivers is the validity of those terms, not a test against nature. \textsf{[REAL, scope]} The result follows from $\Omega$ being fixed by the light and from the corner being a rank-one projection: it holds for any unit vector fixed by the flow; the lemma does not relate the two faces by a map between the spaces.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The lemma of the two faces.} \textsf{[REAL]} \texttt{the\_psion\_is\_the\_corner\_on\_both\_faces}: on both faces the psion is the unit vector whose corner is the projector onto it; the corner scalarises; it weighs $1$; and the motor compressed by the corner returns the corner. On the concrete face, $\texttt{psionCorner.p}=|\Phi^{+}\rangle\langle\Phi^{+}|$. "
             r"The link is one of \emph{structure}, not of vectors: the Fock vacuum $\Omega$ and the Bell vector $\Phi^{+}$ live in distinct spaces (one of infinite dimension; $\mathbb{C}^{4}$) and \emph{are not identified}. "
             r"The key \texttt{testemunha\_estatica\_v396.fock\_face.linked\_to\_the\_corner\_by\_a\_lemma} was the literal \texttt{False} from v396 to v406 (erratum E18, in its own name: it recorded the state of that time); in v407 it is read from the kernel of the rite itself and in this rite it reads " + _b407(_ch407.get("testemunha_estatica_v396.fock_face.linked_to_the_corner_by_a_lemma")) + r". "
             r"Where the v396 and v406 sections of this paper and the sealed records \texttt{testemunha\_estatica\_v396}, \texttt{cunhagens\_v396} and \texttt{fechamento\_v406} say, in the present tense, that no lemma links \texttt{psion C} to the \texttt{psionCorner}, read: it was the state of the date; the current reading is this one; the sealed texts stay as a record (E20 for the two checks that demanded the false).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The pair.} \textsf{[ONTO]} The operator (our translation): the graviton is the bound state of two psions, so they never cancel, because they stand for the very irresolvable tension in the plane, so that its reading is made through the graviton (phase and return of phase); and, as to the corner, I think it is the 4x4 projector (please check). "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The stone \texttt{Par} checks it, composing only terms the kernel already had: the pair is \emph{bound} (\texttt{psionCorner} is the shadow of the graviton; the entanglement is the Half-Nat, $\mathrm{CCI}=\tfrac12$; the product, not bound, has $\mathrm{CCI}=0$); it \emph{never cancels} (it is idempotent with trace $1$; the individual does not echo: the marginal is $\tfrac12$ of the identity); the reading is the doubled phase of the helicity $\pm2$ ($e_{+}$ turns by $2\theta$) and the return of phase is the half-turn $\theta=\pi$; and the corner is the $4\times4$ projector (the $2\times2$ matrix of the numeric stone 92\_ is the face of \emph{one} psion). "
             r"The 2025 ACOM/INPI text, which gave the pair as cancelled into vacuum, and the Frontier sentence of 02/2026, which gave the graviton as a non-entangled product, are superseded by this coinage; they stay beside it as a record (E19).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the lemma and the pair do NOT claim.} \textsf{[OPEN]} The pair of psions on the \emph{Fock face} (two psions over the vacuum, $a^{\dagger}a^{\dagger}|0\rangle$) remains open: the Fock certificate has no creation operators as a term. \textsf{[REAL, scope]} The Bell space ($\mathbb{C}^{2}\otimes\mathbb{C}^{2}$) and the TT sector of the linearised spin~2 ($\mathbb{R}^{4}$) are distinct spaces: the stone \texttt{Par} juxtaposes the bound face and the helicity face, and the conjunction is not an identification; the bridge between them is not a term [ONTO]. "
             r"\textsf{[OPEN/KNOWN]} $K(O)\neq\bot$ for compact $O$ remains unproved: only on the wedge. The psion of the 2025 archive ($a^{\dagger}|0\rangle$) and the psion of the kernel (\texttt{psion C = C.Omega}, the vacuum itself) are readings of different dates; the newest coinage holds for the kernel term.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The seven stones of 02/11, with the operator's names.} \textsf{[REAL]} Each compiles in the trio and carries its own reservations in its docstring. The bridge of friction is trivial by definition (the temperature $1/P=\kappa/2\pi$ is the normalisation inherited by the kernel, without Unruh/KMS). K is the tangent: in every transition $\theta=\pi/4$ is a theorem, so $K=1$ always; the content is the form $\text{mass}=\text{projection}/K$. The inscribed One is the only \emph{fixed} vector of the light in the concrete Fock space, with $B_0$ read as the boost of the light [KNOWN, to be checked]; an eigenvector with a phase is not excluded by a term; the reading of the inscribed One as the vacuum is the operator's [ONTO] (02/11, quoted in the stone). The key of the guard acts on the form, and the inverse is algebraic, not a physical channel. The guard: K alone does not refuse. The preserved reading: the form is rebuilt, and the inverse amplifies. The Equal: the Hubble ratio obeys the laws of the equals sign; reading K as the graviton is the operator's [ONTO]. "
             r"\textsf{[DECLARADO]} Three of them (\texttt{KEhATangente}, \texttt{APonteDoAtrito}, \texttt{OUmInscrito}) were reviewed by Sonnet on 02/11; all nine were checked by the third-party reviewer of this preparation on 03/11 (\texttt{\#print axioms} in the trio, diff against the origins and docstrings; not the proofs line by line; 0 high and 0 medium in every round; the low remarks stay written in the review notebook).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What stays out, stated.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The continuous motor in the quantum pillar \emph{does not enter} (D38): the operator said (our translation) that he wants observable content, because to him it is the holographic bath, it is dark energy itself at work, but he has not yet managed to explain precisely what he wants; the saying is recorded as a coinage [ONTO], without a term and without a test. "
             r"The test (d) of branch B of the ringdown enters only by \emph{citation} of the V1.1 pre-registration (manifest whose sha256 begins with \texttt{" + _tx407(_td407.get("manifesto_sha16")) + r"}); by the operator's option (c), if the test has no power he will not insert it in the um.py: no result, no run on real data. The planning power (3.7 to 3.9$\sigma$ with ten events; 2.1 to 3.2$\sigma$ with the uncertainty of the apparatus bias) stays below $5\sigma$: a measured wall, not a falsification. The app and the JEV contract are updated by the chain (step S10 of the orchestrator), outside the program.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the record checks in this rite.} \textsf{[REAL]} \texttt{psion\_canto\_v407}: anchors ok " + _i407(_v407.get("n_ancoras_ok")) + r"/" + _i407(_v407.get("n_ancoras")) + r"; bundle modules with the pinned sha256 " + _i407(_v407.get("n_modulos_ok")) + r"/" + _i407(_v407.get("n_modulos")) + r"; flags True " + _i407(_v407.get("n_flags_true")) + r"/" + _i407(_v407.get("n_flags")) + r"; the key of the lemma, read from the kernel: " + _b407(_f407.get("link_read_from_the_kernel")) + r"; the gate of this rite has the same verdict as the sealed v406. Verdict: \texttt{" + _tx407(_f407.get("verdict")) + r"}. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} What changed in the old records is \emph{only what they read}; no sealed text was rewritten. \textsf{[OPEN]} What nature decides stays with nature: $\beta$ at $5\sigma$; no new data enters here. The names of the stones are the operator's. Kernel validity is not creditation; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never confirmation; the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\medskip\hrule\medskip")
